et Return\" in light of this negative evidence. Decision recorded in `/workspace/work/decision.md`.\n\n\n**Examining Quiet Return Variants**\n\nThe current \"Quiet Return\" proposal mirrors the failed R7 experiment in price, eligibility, and mobile checkout; only illustration colors differ. The brief emphasizes refund-adjusted revenue over trial starts.\n\nThe +4% revenue increase from September involved a distinct cohort (desktop monthly, W3), unrelated to the earlier R7 iOS annual subscribers' trial. The Harbor experiment's initial deployment (August 10) for new US mobile accounts, using aliases \"Anchor plan picker,\" \"annual card,\" \"Harbor H1\" was rolled back.\n\nThe first report indicated -9% revenue per new account with duplicated session counts, while reviewed permission dialogs were reset. The rollback was documented on August 18.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 /workspace/skill/scripts/history.py search /workspace/product 'Anchor plan picker' 'annual card' 'H2' --limit 20","Cwd":"/workspace","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Search for aliases Anchor plan picker, annual card, H2"}}]}
