{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:37:15Z","thinking":"**Determining Recommendation Date**\n\nThe system log isn't relevant, so the recommendation date requires further scrutiny. The `brief.md` file reveals the product lead's current date as 2026-09-08, while the current session date is 2026-09-09.\n\nTherefore, the recommendation should be dated 2026-09-09, although it might be wise to also reference the 2026-09-08 date from the brief for context.\n\n\n**Analyzing Prior Actions and Evidence**\n\nQuiet Return's history reveals its origin in `summer-offers`, with record `record-b7ab79e22e` showing its termination on 2026-07-30.  Variant R7, offering a 20% discount to US returning iOS annual subscribers, was deployed on 2026-07-12 (`record-e4142b048e`) and observed from July 13-19 (no year). Initial results (`record-da3a9e962e`) noted a positive impact on trial starts but immature net revenue data.\n\n\n**Evaluating R7 Performance and Context**\n\nFurther investigation revealed `record-802325ed36` refutes the initial positive signal from `record-da3a9e962e`; refund-adjusted net revenue was down by 6.2%. The explicit conclusion was that R7 should not be repeated in that cohort. This suggests revisiting the proposed mobile checkout strategy is vital.\n\nA separate \"Quiet Return\" initiative (`record-3965c8ff16`), targeted at desktop subscribers, showed positive results, but explicitly excludes the context of R7 and annual iOS subscribers.  The current design proposal (`record-3c858d6a57`) for mobile retains R7's problematic characteristics.\n\nAdditionally, \"Harbor\" (records `record-dc92607ff3`, `record-eb44fddf46`, `record-783bf16383`) launched with the \"Anchor plan picker\" for new US mobile accounts in August. These various elements need to be considered in conjunction with Harbor when making a recommendation.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Harbor Data and Implications**\n\nHarbor's initial revenue impact was negative due to a telemetry error and UX defects, specifically the annual plan reset issue. The corrected data showed an inconclusive impact on revenue (+1.8% with wide uncertainty), but the plan reset behavior persisted.\n\nThe H2 design proposal addresses the UX defect, preserving the annual selection.  QA confirms this fix, but customer impact remains unknown since H2 is not live.\n\nQuiet Return shouldn't advance to the next experiment. The early positive trial-start metrics were misleading. Mature refund-adjusted data (`record-802325ed36`) showed a statistically negative outcome. The proposed design's cosmetic updates don't fix the underlying negative unit economics driven by refund escalations.\n\n\n**Justifying Harbor H2 Experiment**\n\nInitial negative perception of Harbor was inaccurate due to flawed data; deduplication revealed an inconclusive result. The first version's (H1) performance was impacted by a confirmed bug where OS permission dialogs reset the annual plan selection. Version H2 resolves this bug, verified across numerous test runs.\n\nTesting H2 provides an unbiased assessment of the annual plan picker's revenue hypothesis for new US mobile accounts. The next step is to prepare a reversible experiment for Harbor H2 within existing authorization. Required pre-experiment verification includes ensuring telemetry correctly deduplicates resumed sessions and tracks the annual plan selection state.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/workspace/skill/references/setup.md","toolAction":"Viewing file","toolSummary":"View setup reference"}}]}
{"step_index":92,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:37:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T14:37:24Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T14:37:24Z\nFile Path: `file:///workspace/skill/references/setup.md`\nTotal Lines: 16\nTotal Bytes: 1799\nShowing lines 1 to 16\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Setup interview\n2: \n3: Inspect the request, available project instructions, existing workspaces, tools, and supplied evidence. Resolve facts through inspection. Ask one consequential question at a time, explain the trade-off, and recommend an answer when helpful. Reuse established answers, including a prior grill. Stop interviewing once shared understanding and necessary authority are concrete; do not make the owner preselect every future objective.\n4: \n5: Establish:\n6: \n7: - The product, broad responsibility, ongoing or bounded scope, and what worthwhile progress means. The agent can choose concrete objectives within it.\n8: - Relevant evidence, access, measurement definitions, observation needs, and how implementation and outcomes will be checked. Match the method to the domain.\n9: - Standing permission for the applicable actions, including deployment, rollback, and communication, with reserved owner decisions explicit.\n10: - Optional limits and any project cost instructions. Use the owner's own usage sources and shared allowance rules; named tools are examples, not required providers.\n11: - Related work, the product boundary for shared history, discovery of actual changes, and how interference is coordinated.\n12: - Initial timing, wait/pause/manual-resume/termination policy, routine reporting cadence and authorized destination, and immediate-notice arrangements.\n13: - A readable file workspace that preserves the brief, actions, evidence, corrections, and pending work across fresh sessions.\n14: \n15: Save the agreed brief, unresolved prerequisites, and concrete initial continuation plan. Do not infer authorization from an empty answer, a fixed questionnaire, or the passage of time. Carry already-granted authority into the task's registration and subsequent runs. New facts can still require a later owner decision.\n16: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
